{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789661310,"nonce":"255oPI7aYKwUuoKPKwzNlQteW6I=","title":"Sync policy: bidirectional, 3-way per field, Jira wins on conflict","message":"Decided: true bidirectional; Jira is canonical company-wide.\n- Per field, 3-way merge against the last-synced value (recorded in sync metadata): only one side changed -\u003e apply it; both changed -\u003e Jira wins, and the overridden local value is recorded on the issue (comment or metadata) so nothing is lost silently.\n- New local issue -\u003e created in Jira on next sync; key becomes an alias.\n- Jira delete -\u003e local move to canceled category + metadata, never a local rm.\n- Identities: Jira accountId \u003c-\u003e identity via the existing LoginMetaKey pattern; create identities for unknown Jira users.\nWrite this down in doc/design before implementing; the bridge core `since`-timestamp loop stays.","files":null}]}